EXAMPLE 1.5. Let $\Delta = \{0, 1, 2, 3\}$ and let $\mathcal{D}$ be the family of all non-empty subsets of $\Delta$.

The development is with the [four-token powerset](1980_P4.md) peer.

<!-- formalization -->

**Theorem (`example_1_5`).** There is a neighbourhood system on four tokens whose neighbourhoods are exactly the nonempty subsets.

*Proof.* By the four-token neighbourhood system. ∎
